<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>ai.ted.backup</string>

  <!-- Takes one verified copy of everything that cannot be rebuilt, daily at
       04:00, and prunes to the newest 14. T05 asks for a defined cadence, and
       until this existed the only backup that had ever been taken was taken by
       hand, which is a cadence of "whenever somebody remembers".

       04:00 because the gateway is quietest then and the SQLite online backup
       reads through the same locking the gateway uses: it is safe at any hour,
       but a quiet hour finishes faster. RunAtLoad is deliberately false. A
       backup on every login would fill the disk with near-identical copies and
       push the older, differently-shaped ones out of the retention window.

       It never restores. Restoring is a decision a person makes, never a thing
       a timer does at four in the morning.

       The interpreter is the Hermes venv's, not /usr/bin/python3, and that is
       not a preference. macOS refuses a launchd agent access to ~/Documents
       unless that binary has been granted it, and the Command Line Tools
       python has not: the first scheduled run failed with "Operation not
       permitted" before it could read its own script. ai.ted.gatewatch has run
       321 times from the same directory using this interpreter. Nothing here
       needs the venv's packages; it needs its permission. -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Users/vandana.agarwal/.hermes/hermes-agent/venv/bin/python3</string>
    <string>/Users/vandana.agarwal/Documents/build-week-health accountability partner/scripts/ted-backup.py</string>
  </array>

  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Hour</key>
    <integer>4</integer>
    <key>Minute</key>
    <integer>0</integer>
  </dict>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/vandana.agarwal/.hermes/logs/ted-backup.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/vandana.agarwal/.hermes/logs/ted-backup.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
